WEBVTT

00:12.490 --> 00:15.290
Flagship of Torpedo Squadron 2, Yahagi.

00:15.810 --> 00:17.080
Oh, come in.

00:17.740 --> 00:19.370
Yahagi, coming in.

00:38.470 --> 00:45.130
<b>See You Again on Another Quiet Blue Sea</b>

02:06.100 --> 02:10.520
<b>Naval Interception Mission</b>

02:10.940 --> 02:12.770
What?!

02:12.770 --> 02:17.860
I heard at 6th Fleet Command 
that the message was received.

02:17.860 --> 02:19.440
It's true, it seems.

02:17.860 --> 02:23.830
<b>Tone</b>

02:23.830 --> 02:26.160
Tone, calm down.

02:26.160 --> 02:27.820
I <i>am</i> calm!

02:27.820 --> 02:29.620
I need to get going!

02:35.260 --> 02:37.330
Oh? Aoba saw it!

02:37.330 --> 02:38.780
My chance for a scoop!

02:38.780 --> 02:40.930
Knock it off, "This is the Aoba"!

02:40.930 --> 02:43.040
Don't call me that.

02:53.150 --> 02:57.370
Looks like we'll have to join in the fun.

02:57.370 --> 02:58.860
Right, Haruna?

03:03.570 --> 03:05.780
Haruna is just fine.

03:05.780 --> 03:08.620
What are you so down about?

03:08.620 --> 03:12.580
Ise and Hyuuga's Operation 
Kita Completion Force

03:12.580 --> 03:16.430
made it all the way from Syonan 
to Taiwan. It's a miracle.

03:16.430 --> 03:19.260
And they're loaded with 
valuable fuel and materials...

03:21.220 --> 03:23.340
They sent a message saying that your sister,

03:23.340 --> 03:28.620
the one who'd taken a torpedo on the way 
home from Leyte and barely survived,

03:28.620 --> 03:30.350
made it to Taiwan, too.

03:32.190 --> 03:37.620
Yup. The Completion Force 
stopped by where Takao is

03:37.620 --> 03:40.400
and said that Kongou's recovering nicely.

03:40.880 --> 03:42.990
She's tough.

03:43.650 --> 03:45.310
Really?

03:46.250 --> 03:47.700
I'm so glad...

03:48.610 --> 03:52.420
She didn't take any unnecessary risks. 
Instead, she retreated to Taiwan.

03:52.420 --> 03:54.920
You should thank Urakaze, her escort.

03:55.860 --> 03:56.860
Yes...

03:57.600 --> 04:00.130
Sister Kongou...

04:02.890 --> 04:04.090
Here.

04:04.090 --> 04:06.460
Eat up for now.

04:06.460 --> 04:08.280
While you've still got the chance, I mean.

04:08.280 --> 04:10.490
The last battle will be soon.

04:13.170 --> 04:14.190
Yes.

04:21.300 --> 04:22.700
Thanks.

04:25.040 --> 04:28.870
Yahagicchi from Sasebo was saying...

04:28.870 --> 04:32.250
Yup. The mission begins soon.

04:32.930 --> 04:37.590
Which means if everyone from Operation 
Kita comes back with enough supplies

04:37.590 --> 04:41.710
to solve the fuel shortage here at Kure...

04:41.710 --> 04:43.670
Yup.

04:44.060 --> 04:47.890
Kure will send out Yamato.

04:47.890 --> 04:51.220
And our admiral...

04:51.220 --> 04:52.620
...will do the same.

04:53.690 --> 04:57.610
I was lucky enough to be born. So...

04:57.610 --> 04:58.880
I want to go, too.

05:07.890 --> 05:08.920
Yamato...

05:12.620 --> 05:15.410
That concludes the mission preparations!

05:18.400 --> 05:22.500
Mogami, how are your Kai-Ni upgrades 
and new flight equipment?

05:23.590 --> 05:24.930
Just fine!

05:24.930 --> 05:27.030
The catapult's feeling great.

05:27.450 --> 05:29.300
And your new planes?

05:29.300 --> 05:32.130
I was given 951 Kyoufuus.

05:32.130 --> 05:35.540
As well as what's left of the 
634th Air Unit, and ace Zuiuns...

05:40.920 --> 05:44.650
The Zuiuns and Kyoufuu 
are both up to full strength.

05:44.650 --> 05:49.910
Actually, now that I'm Kai-Ni, I can carry more than before.

05:49.910 --> 05:51.310
And they're better trained.

05:51.310 --> 05:52.240
I'm ready.

05:53.380 --> 05:54.380
Good.

05:57.020 --> 05:59.270
As for the operation target,

05:59.270 --> 06:03.170
our Type 2 Large Flying Boats and
 Saiuns say that the invasion force

06:03.690 --> 06:08.970
has left port and is heading 
for the Nansei Islands.

06:10.170 --> 06:14.090
The Completion Force, including Ise and 
Hyuuga, is already near the mainland,

06:14.090 --> 06:18.060
and will bring valuable fuel 
from Syonan directly to Kure.

06:18.480 --> 06:22.350
We will not be waiting for their escorts 
in Destroyer Division 21 to return to base.

06:22.350 --> 06:24.920
Instead, Torpedo Squadron 2 will 
launch all its available forces,

06:24.920 --> 06:27.260
as well as aviation cruiser Mogami,

06:27.260 --> 06:29.660
to intercept their force.

06:29.660 --> 06:34.380
So, we'll be launching a valiant 
attack on the enemy invasion force, right?

06:34.380 --> 06:35.400
No.

06:36.680 --> 06:37.550
What?

06:41.060 --> 06:42.020
Then...

06:48.240 --> 06:49.340
Here you go.

06:49.340 --> 06:52.220
I was just hungry. Spa...

06:53.430 --> 06:54.520
They're back.

06:55.310 --> 06:57.690
The Completion Force is back.

07:05.500 --> 07:09.160
Hey! We're back!

07:11.660 --> 07:14.110
Yeah. I guess we are.

07:16.070 --> 07:19.120
Operation Kita was a success...

07:20.450 --> 07:22.130
I'm so glad.

07:30.050 --> 07:33.280
If we're not taking out the invasion force,

07:33.280 --> 07:36.390
then what <i>is</i> our mission, exactly?

07:36.840 --> 07:40.600
The invasion force is being supported 
by a powerful enemy carrier fleet.

07:40.980 --> 07:45.540
It's split into three groups and
 is advancing ahead of them.

07:45.540 --> 07:48.940
So the enemy's already reorganized 
and replaced their losses?

07:49.380 --> 07:52.770
Direct support from three carrier groups...

07:52.770 --> 07:54.780
That'll be tough.

07:55.270 --> 07:59.700
Yes. Our own carrier fleet 
is still being rebuilt.

08:00.210 --> 08:02.090
And what's worse...

08:02.970 --> 08:05.860
A surface strike force primarily 
composed of enemy battleships

08:05.860 --> 08:08.690
supporting the invasion 
of the southwest islands

08:08.690 --> 08:10.880
is charting a course through this area.

08:11.460 --> 08:13.650
Excuse me for saying so, Yahagi, but...

08:13.650 --> 08:15.930
There's no way we can win this, right?

08:17.340 --> 08:19.970
I'm afraid you're right.

08:20.810 --> 08:22.370
What does that mean?

08:20.810 --> 08:22.370
But then, how...

08:22.370 --> 08:23.440
Silence!

08:23.790 --> 08:27.960
I'm afraid that even with 
all our available strength,

08:28.540 --> 08:31.020
even with our aces in Torpedo Squadron 2,

08:31.020 --> 08:36.200
it's suicide to take this enemy head-on.

08:36.900 --> 08:40.410
However, Ise, Hyuuga, and the rest of 
the Completion Force of Operation Kita

08:40.410 --> 08:43.500
have succeeded in their mission.

08:44.030 --> 08:48.840
They brought strategic materials 
from the south to Kure,

08:48.840 --> 08:51.000
especially precious fuel!

08:51.000 --> 08:54.760
Kure will be sending Yamato,

08:54.760 --> 08:58.720
our one active carrier, Ryuuhou,

08:59.410 --> 09:02.680
Hibiki and Hatsushimo, 
who were delivering messages to Kure,

09:03.050 --> 09:05.300
as well as Carrier Division 4 
and Ooyodo's group,

09:05.300 --> 09:07.810
who unfortunately will 
not be getting any rest.

09:08.360 --> 09:11.860
Additionally, what remains of 
Destroyer Division 7 will be their escorts.

09:25.380 --> 09:26.700
Mission time, right?

09:26.700 --> 09:28.580
With master!

09:30.540 --> 09:32.440
Eat this!

09:34.770 --> 09:36.000
Guys...

09:38.790 --> 09:40.110
Thank you so much!

09:45.430 --> 09:49.770
These ships will be coming to Sasebo 
to reinforce us after refueling.

09:50.370 --> 09:51.980
Until they arrive...

09:51.980 --> 09:56.190
Torpedo Squadron 2 will engage 
in a naval interception mission.

09:56.750 --> 09:58.780
A naval interception mission?

09:58.780 --> 10:04.540
<b>Supply Fleet</b>

09:59.220 --> 10:00.660
Our objective is here.

10:01.630 --> 10:05.680
Torpedo Squadron 2 will launch in force,

10:06.380 --> 10:08.750
and use our high speed 
and the cover of night

10:09.230 --> 10:15.240
to find and engage the enemy supply
 fleet behind the carrier groups!

10:15.240 --> 10:18.430
If possible, we will make multiple 
attacks to destroy them!

10:18.980 --> 10:25.390
Our land-based aircraft will provide air 
cover and support as best they're able.

10:27.770 --> 10:29.530
We are Torpedo Squadron 2!

10:29.530 --> 10:31.280
We're not going to our deaths.

10:31.280 --> 10:33.330
We're fighting to carry on!

10:33.910 --> 10:35.030
Yes, ma'am!

10:35.850 --> 10:36.870
We're counting on you!

10:38.790 --> 10:41.620
We'll be launching tomorrow at 1600.

10:41.620 --> 10:43.540
Everyone be ready!

10:43.540 --> 10:44.450
Dismissed!

10:52.830 --> 10:55.090
Shigure, a moment, if you would.

11:09.310 --> 11:11.490
Um...

11:17.090 --> 11:18.360
Me?

11:19.250 --> 11:20.270
Yes.

11:38.890 --> 11:43.140
Interception Force, Torpedo Squadron 2, 
raise anchor and set out!

11:48.750 --> 11:53.940
Interception Force, Modified 
Aviation Cruiser Mogami, setting out!

11:57.930 --> 11:58.960
Here we go!

12:03.410 --> 12:05.700
Destroyer Division 41, setting out!

12:05.700 --> 12:07.410
Destroyer Division 17, here we go.

12:07.950 --> 12:09.160
Ready to go.

12:09.160 --> 12:10.620
All set!

12:11.130 --> 12:13.820
Torpedo Squadron 2, 
Destroyer Division 17, set out!

12:22.540 --> 12:24.260
Be on high alert for submarines!

12:24.260 --> 12:25.500
I'll take the lead!

12:25.500 --> 12:28.500
Fleet, take Diamond Formation 
centered around Mogami!

12:28.500 --> 12:29.540
Roger!

12:29.540 --> 12:30.610
Roger!

12:37.930 --> 12:40.570
I feel like I'm Yamato!

12:40.570 --> 12:42.280
Don't be stupid!

12:42.280 --> 12:44.460
There's no time for idle chit-chat.

12:45.480 --> 12:47.230
We'll engage the enemy at first light.

12:47.230 --> 12:50.390
I want to avoid air attacks 
and be back by dawn.

12:51.500 --> 12:54.100
Mogami, launch night recon planes!

12:54.100 --> 12:54.920
Go for it!

12:54.920 --> 12:56.140
Roger!

12:56.140 --> 12:58.420
Launching night recon planes!

13:04.830 --> 13:06.340
Don't let your speed drop!

13:06.340 --> 13:09.100
Prepare to engage the enemy at first light!

13:10.660 --> 13:12.720
Yeah...

13:12.720 --> 13:15.190
I hope that's how it goes...

13:16.900 --> 13:19.380
Ignore any picket ships you encounter.

13:19.380 --> 13:21.780
Get right up close against 
the enemy supply fleet.

13:22.430 --> 13:26.860
If we encounter any surface ships, shift to 
Line Ahead Formation and engage!

13:26.860 --> 13:27.640
Sounds great...

13:27.170 --> 13:28.660
Roger!

13:27.640 --> 13:28.660
...to me!

13:39.710 --> 13:44.880
I wish I could've gone with 
Yuki and Mogami...

13:44.880 --> 13:46.650
Don't be silly.

13:48.290 --> 13:52.010
Mogami was telling me
 about you, the... old guy?

13:52.010 --> 13:54.180
Don't call me that.

13:55.380 --> 13:57.320
Um...

13:57.320 --> 13:58.650
Sorry.

13:58.650 --> 14:00.730
This is only happening 
because the admiral

14:00.730 --> 14:04.990
and the flagship of Torpedo 
Squadron 2 really wanted it done.

14:06.830 --> 14:07.950
Are you ready?

14:07.950 --> 14:09.940
We're all set!

14:11.410 --> 14:14.970
Of course, Shigure, this is only possible 
because of your experience,

14:14.970 --> 14:17.370
success in combat, and training.

14:18.220 --> 14:21.530
Everything you have right now 
is what made this possible.

14:22.410 --> 14:23.570
You're sure?

14:24.180 --> 14:25.260
Of course.

14:34.890 --> 14:36.020
Admiral?

14:37.450 --> 14:40.300
Shigure, there's no changing the past.

14:44.310 --> 14:50.480
But seeing the past for what it truly is 
can help us change the future.

14:53.460 --> 14:54.540
Shigure.

14:56.030 --> 14:59.030
Your third modification. Shigure Kai-san.

14:59.760 --> 15:00.860
You're okay with this, right?

15:11.990 --> 15:13.050
Yes.

15:15.810 --> 15:18.660
Night attackers ready for launch!

15:19.670 --> 15:22.190
Attackers, take off!

15:22.190 --> 15:25.690
Roger! Night Zuiun, take off!

15:42.310 --> 15:45.670
Okay, we are entering enemy range.

15:45.670 --> 15:47.630
Vanguard Formation, everyone.

15:47.630 --> 15:49.570
Destroyer Division 17, roger.

15:49.570 --> 15:51.400
Destroyer Division 41, roger.

16:20.800 --> 16:22.030
Here I go.

17:00.560 --> 17:02.190
Hang onto this for me.

17:13.610 --> 17:17.780
<i>Initiating third-stage modifications 
for Shiratsuyu Class Destroyer Shigure.</i>

17:18.360 --> 17:22.770
<i>Initiating third-stage modifications 
for Shiratsuyu Class Destroyer Shigure.</i>

17:23.600 --> 17:27.790
<i>Initiating third-stage modifications 
for Shiratsuyu Class Destroyer Shigure.</i>

17:32.020 --> 17:32.950
They're in range!

17:32.950 --> 17:34.820
Line Ahead, everyone!

17:36.630 --> 17:39.070
Mogami, have the ones 
closest fire signal flares.

17:39.070 --> 17:40.330
Roger!

17:40.330 --> 17:41.910
Fire signal flares!

17:47.270 --> 17:49.790
Night attackers! Tora! Tora! Tora!

18:49.640 --> 18:53.440
Multiple enemy escorts incoming off 
to the port side to our front!

18:54.610 --> 18:56.070
Enemy has opened fire!

19:01.950 --> 19:04.950
All ships, charge! After me!

19:09.670 --> 19:11.500
Hamakaze's been hit and
 took moderate damage!

19:11.500 --> 19:13.100
Send her to dock 3!

19:13.100 --> 19:14.950
Pump her out as soon as she's inside!

19:24.140 --> 19:25.930
Admiral, old man...

19:25.930 --> 19:28.650
I'm sorry, but Suzutsuki 
has taken light damage, too.

19:28.650 --> 19:30.100
Look after her!

19:30.560 --> 19:32.300
Open up dock 3!

19:32.300 --> 19:35.570
Suzutsuki! Light damage! Emergency repairs!

19:42.940 --> 19:50.210
Admiral, Torpedo Squadron 2 has returned 
from our naval interception mission.

19:50.710 --> 19:51.790
Welcome back.

19:52.630 --> 19:53.930
Combat report.

19:54.370 --> 19:58.270
We sunk three Wa-Class supply ships 
and critically damaged another two.

19:58.270 --> 20:01.880
We sunk four destroyers and 
critically damaged multiple others.

20:01.880 --> 20:07.420
Our own Hamakaze was moderately damaged, 
and Suzutsuki was lightly damaged.

20:08.370 --> 20:10.640
Five of Mogami's air units did not return.

20:11.210 --> 20:12.210
I see.

20:13.500 --> 20:16.140
Admiral, the enemy is in chaos.

20:16.960 --> 20:20.780
As soon as Suzutsuki's emergency repairs 
are completed and Mogami gets new planes,

20:20.780 --> 20:22.950
we'll launch another attack.

20:22.950 --> 20:26.320
But Hamakaze's anchor...

20:26.320 --> 20:28.410
It'll take a long time to repair!

20:29.540 --> 20:31.550
No, it's fine.

20:33.100 --> 20:34.960
That's why we've got...

20:35.490 --> 20:36.780
Sasebo's...

20:38.170 --> 20:39.520
Shigure!

20:51.380 --> 20:54.140
I'll go!

20:55.010 --> 20:56.230
Shigure...

20:56.730 --> 21:00.690
Wow! Gure, you're so cool!

21:02.890 --> 21:05.410
You've still got a lot to do first, right?

21:08.200 --> 21:09.410
Shigure...

21:20.660 --> 21:23.110
Admiral. Yahagi.

21:25.120 --> 21:26.230
Thank you.

21:30.610 --> 21:36.140
I'll join Torpedo Squadron 2's 
next interception mission.

21:37.090 --> 21:38.560
You will launch at...

21:38.560 --> 21:42.860
The enemy's on guard! It'll be dangerous!

21:44.260 --> 21:45.780
I know.

21:46.880 --> 21:54.400
But I'm Shigure, Shiratsuyu-class 
Destroyer with Torpedo Squadron 2.

21:57.610 --> 21:58.670
I'll go.

23:27.460 --> 23:29.800
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.390 --> 23:39.980
<b>See You Again on Another Quiet Blue Sea</b>

23:35.950 --> 23:38.310
Please, remember.
